  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 534 PM MDT Thu Aug 6 2026/ \n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nAs the upper-level ridge continues to move east it will start to\nflatten out allowing hot and dry conditions to persist across \nthe region. Winds will pick up during the peak mixing hours of the\nafternoon, especially across Southwest Montana which will increase\nfire weather concerns through the weekend. Quasi-zonal flow will\nstick around through the middle of next week with some passing\nweak shortwaves possible starting on Monday which may come with a\nlow chance for light precipitation.\n\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nWildfire Smoke:\n\nSmoke from wildfires across the PacNW and Montana will continue to\nimpact air quality for our region, especially in Southwest Montana\nwhere an Air Quality Alert is currently in effect. For most of \nCentral and North-Central Montana significant reductions in air \nquality are not currently expected but could be enough to impact \nthose who are the most sensitive. Those who are particularly \nsensitive to reduced air quality should limit time outdoors and \ntake preventative measures to ensure their safety.\n\n\nHot, Dry, Breezy Friday/Saturday:\n\nAbove normal temperatures will continue through the next week but\nthe hottest temperatures for this forecast period are expected on\nFriday and Saturday with highs reaching into the upper 90s for\nsome locations. Similarly, very dry conditions are expected to\npersist through the weekend across the region which will lead to\nenhanced to critical fire weather concerns (detailed in the FIRE\nWEATHER section).\n\n\nPrecipitation Chances Next Week:\n\nOver the course of the next week a few weak passing shortwaves may\nprovide a chances for precipitation but there is still \nsignificant deviation in the models on how these waves will play \nout and whether or not there is even much of a chance for wetting \nrainfall. It will be something to watch as any amount of \nprecipitation would be welcomed but even if these showers trend on\nthe wetter side it will likely be little relief to the bigger \npicture of our fire weather concerns through the next week. -thor",
